          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What security standards guide your data sanitization in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS implements data sanitization aligned with NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 guidelines, DoD 5220.22-M benchmarks, and HIPAA technical safeguard requirements. Every project includes comprehensive, serialized documentation verifying the permanent erasure or physical shredding of sensitive digital media for Bakersfield enterprises."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What service areas do you cover across Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide scheduled pickups throughout Bakersfield, Oildale, Rosedale, Downtown, and the Stockdale corridor, extending to surrounding Kern County business districts like Shafter, Wasco, and Delano. Our logistics fleet coordinates seamlessly near State Route 99, Highway 58, and Interstate 5."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup service free for Bakersfield businesses?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS provides zero-cost pickup for qualifying volumes of commercial IT assets, desktop fleets, and networking infrastructure across Bakersfield and Kern County. Our team handles complete logistics, secure loading, and chain of custody tracking without assessment fees for qualifying enterprise partners."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide official audit documentation for e-waste disposal?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Following downstream processing, clients receive detailed Certificates of Destruction and serialized asset manifests. These records provide verifiable documentation for California DTSC environmental audits, corporate governance reviews, and industry compliance verifications in Bakersfield."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is your healthcare data destruction HIPAA compliant?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS delivers HIPAA-compliant sanitization designed for healthcare networks like Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield. We execute formal Business Associate Agreements and provide serialized destruction records to ensure complete protected health information (PHI) privacy and audit readiness."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you coordinate large-scale enterprise refreshes in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our nationwide logistics network and 200,000 sq ft processing capacity readily support large-scale enterprise refreshes, multi-facility school district replacements, and extensive corporate liquidations across the San Joaquin Valley with structured pickup scheduling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where is equipment collected in Bakersfield processed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged locally across Kern County and transported to one of our two certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas, where all data destruction and material recovery takes place."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How can Bakersfield businesses recover value from retired IT assets?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling provides transparent asset remarketing and IT liquidation services to help Bakersfield businesses recover residual capital from retired networking equipment, servers, and laptop fleets through tested remarketing channels."
          }
        }
